# Korean Spell Check
## What this skill does
Perform final Korean proofreading through Bareun Hangul (formerly the PNU
spelling/grammar checker), which incorporates National Institute of Korean
Language-style rules.
- Default entry: https://nara-speller.co.kr/speller/.
- For automation, use the legacy form POST surface
https://nara-speller.co.kr/old_speller/results at low request volume only.
- Split long text into chunks and check sequentially.
- Present each original, suggested correction, and reason.
## Policy first
The legacy surface https://nara-speller.co.kr/old_speller/ states noncommercial
use and free access only for individuals or students. Its robots.txt permits /
but excludes /test_speller/. Use this skill only for user-directed final review,
low-frequency requests, and proofreading documents, email, or READMEs.
Do not use it for bulk batches, SaaS backend integration, or unauthorized resale
or republication inside commercial services. Investigate provider permission or
a paid API agreement first for those uses.
## When to use
- "이 한국어 문장 맞춤법 검사해줘"
- "README 한국어 문장 최종 검수해줘"
- "마크다운 파일 전체에서 띄어쓰기/맞춤법 오류를 잡아줘"
- "AI 교정보다 규칙 기반 한국어 검사기로 한 번 더 확인해줘"
## When not to use
- Bulk transmission of code blocks, logs, or mostly English text.
- Sensitive originals that must not be sent to an external web service.
- Work requiring a commercial bulk-processing API.
## Prerequisites
Internet access, Node.js 20+, and this skill's scripts/korean_spell_check.js
(included on installation).
The commands below use jstack's Node port. The observed Python request behavior in
the following historical notes is provenance, not evidence of current service
availability. The consent boundary and current library API are in `SKILL.md`.
## Verified surface notes
The observed public site was https://nara-speller.co.kr/speller/. Ordinary shell
or Node fetches could receive Cloudflare 403 responses in the tested environment,
while a browser-style User-Agent with Python urllib POST returned actual result
HTML from old_speller/results. The free surface returns HTML; no documented
public JSON API was confirmed.
## Workflow
### 1. Obtain the text or file path
Check directly supplied text. For files, accept UTF-8 text/Markdown. If code
blocks dominate, clarify whether the user wants a narrower scope first.
### 2. Keep requests conservative
Use chunks of about 1500 characters, with at least one second between requests.
Do not process too many files at once.
### 3. Run the helper
```bash
node -- scripts/korean_spell_check.js --file README.md --format json
```
Short text can be supplied with --text:
```bash
node -- scripts/korean_spell_check.js --text "아버지가방에들어가신다." --format text
```
### 4. Return change-focused output
Present the corrected full sentence/paragraph, major changes, and each original,
suggestion, and reason. If needed, explain that results come from a public web
checker and final contextual judgment requires human review.
Example JSON fields (actual Korean correction content):
```json
{
"original": "아버지가방에들어가신다",
"suggestions": ["아버지가 방에 들어가신다"],
"reason": "띄어쓰기, 붙여쓰기, 음절 대치와 같은 교정 방법에 따라 수정한 결과입니다."
}
```
## Done when
The public-surface policy has been checked, long text is chunked, output centers
on original/suggestion/reason, and low-frequency noncommercial scope is clear.
